### What happened?

On `anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5`, pi has no way to run without thinking, even though the Anthropic API does accept `thinking: {type: "disabled"}` on Haiku 5.5.
### Steps to reproduce

```ts
const model = getModel("anthropic", "claude-haiku-5-5");
getSupportedThinkingLevels(model);       // no "off"
streamSimple(model, ctx, { onPayload }); // no reasoning requested
// payload: thinking {type:"adaptive", block_binding:{…}}, output_config {effort:"high"},
//          plus a system message with output_config {effort:"high"}
```

### Expected behavior

Haiku 5.5 lists `off`. When `off` is requested (or no reasoning at all), pi sends `thinking: {type: "disabled"}` with a top-lev
